  "negatives_note": "All three benchmarks define hits by each screen's own significance criterion and score only over genes that screen assayed. Untested genes are absent from the candidate pool rather than labelled negative, which respects the use case's exclusion; the cost is that none of these benchmarks tests whether a method would have found a target outside the pool. Every judgement is proxy. Each protocol carries the hit definition in metric_definition, and the negative definition appears in each dataset's scope_note, each protocol's limitations and each judgement's rationale.",
